{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 65, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 65, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=66&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=64&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 542585287, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542585287-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "I would not go there a second time!", "text": "So for a first time in Kathmandu and if you have a taste for the macabre, yes, it is worth a visit. But the stench of the burning bodies can be brutal. Climb up the stairs on the opposite side of the river and go look at the monkeys play instead. Also a fantastic view of the city from above, including the Boudhanath Stupa! The price you have to pay as a foreigner is off-putting and for this place, NOT worth it. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 2, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "070BFDFADEE4D5889FDF8799169A4FAB", "name": "YNNYN", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/YNNYN", "username": "YNNYN", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/55/09/03/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 174, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187373, "location_name": "Düsseldorf", "location_name_detailed": "Düsseldorf, Germany"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-22", "published_at_date": "2017-11-22"}, {"review_id": 542514339, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542514339-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Dramatic Cultural Experience", "text": "We stayed for the whole afternoon. I had seen a cremation in a small village on a river.\nThis is full on ritual. My local friend asked if this went on in my country. I told him this would land you in jail!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "EFA72A5EA463CE7C485C0EA947BF5B98", "name": "Iratdog", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Iratdog", "username": "Iratdog", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/a4/b6/17/avatar.jpg", "contribution_count": 1282, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 47994, "location_name": "Kerhonkson", "location_name_detailed": "Kerhonkson, New York"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-21", "published_at_date": "2017-11-22"}, {"review_id": 542479077, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542479077-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Fascinating!", "text": "Pashupatina Shiva temple complex is completely fascinating. \nA guide is highly recommended here. \nChoose your guide carefully. Better to go inside and walk around a bit, the right accredited  guide will find you! Our guide was a young, charismatic and very educated young man. \nThe information he gave us was extremely interesting and we felt comfortable to ask him anything. You are in a crematorium basically so it can be quite sensitive. \nWe paid $10 for our guide (1 hour) They will ask for $30 at the entrance\n\nHave since been told it is best to attend early morning or evening prayers here.\n\nBodnath is an easy 20 minute walk from here.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2892C41CCAA9F293B14E41963029D99B", "name": "wendyc2020", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/wendyc2020", "username": "wendyc2020", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/09/02/3c/f8/wendyc2020.jpg", "contribution_count": 184, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 34227, "location_name": "Fort Lauderdale", "location_name_detailed": "Fort Lauderdale, Florida"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-21", "published_at_date": "2017-11-22"}, {"review_id": 542152676, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542152676-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Aarati at 7pm", "text": "Every day in 7 pm aarati is done in Eastern part of pashupatinath temple in bank of bagmati river. This is evening worship of god shiva in pashupatinath temple.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C5AA7A29992F40644D3482703A437B71", "name": "Purna P Paudel", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/paudelpp", "username": "paudelpp", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ec/a2/default-avatar-2020-3.jpg", "contribution_count": 4, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 424935, "location_name": "Birgunj", "location_name_detailed": "Birgunj, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/51/db/af/aarati-time-in-pashupatinath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/51/db/b7/aarati-time-in-pashupatinath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/51/db/bd/aarati-time-in-pashupatinath.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-11-20", "published_at_date": "2017-11-20"}, {"review_id": 542118227, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542118227-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "One of the Big Three tourist attractions", "text": "This temple is a must-do for anyone in Kathmandu, but don't expect huge, impressive monuments. It's a sacred location and a bit of a trek (recommend a guide for tourists) from Thamel, but it's something you'll be glad you did an fought the crowds for. Guides will give a good overview of the history of the place and the development of the whole complex, plus will make it easier with entry tickets, but it's not difficult if you want to go it alone with a Lonely Planet or guidebook. Pashupatinath is a Hindu complex for cremations and worshippers and those dedicated to the faith, so tourists are generally outnumbered by local and visiting Hindus - please be patient and considerate of them when you visit, as they're possibly there for a funeral. \n\nBodies are prepared and cremated in the complex, in the open and in full view of tourists. Respect their procession, keep clear and keep photos to a minimum and from a distance (if you really need to take them at all). Bodies are cremated and collected, but ashes from the pyres are pushed into the river. There's plenty of smoke and debris around the complex too. \n\nThe complex is full of history and has been added to over the years, so there's a variety of smaller temples and monuments, and you could spend either hours here or wrap the whole thing up in 30mins - depends how much you really want to see. On entry there are the standard street vendors and beggars as it's a main tourist hot-spot, but they generally don't hassle as much as those in Thamel. \n\nThere are plenty of animals too, ranging from cows to monkeys to the always common dogs. Take note however that the Sihks who call this place home will really hassle you for money if you take their photo. Some are genuine, some are not, but they all look the part. Make sure you get a price up front if you want to take their photo because they are relentless if you do it the other way around. They make for great photos, so if you can get them at a good price it'll be worth it.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CE2F15F7D33AEEC87709A08DF01CBBA7", "name": "Will L", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/372willl", "username": "372willl", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/7c/01/default-avatar-2020-5.jpg", "contribution_count": 38, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255406, "location_name": "Port Augusta", "location_name_detailed": "Port Augusta, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/51/9d/3e/temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-11-20", "published_at_date": "2017-11-20"}, {"review_id": 542009017, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r542009017-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Nepalese Varanasi", "text": "Hindu Temple to Shiva, with cremation ghats along the river.  .    Rishi's smoking hashish all day, and many elderly residents. Only Hindus are allowed in the main temple, but the grounds are really interesting, Not to be missed.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C597A0E376F584D1D8228FE27A6735D3", "name": "babydragon00", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/babydragon00", "username": "babydragon00", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/7c/01/default-avatar-2020-5.jpg", "contribution_count": 20, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187070, "location_name": "France", "location_name_detailed": "France"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-19", "published_at_date": "2017-11-20"}, {"review_id": 541955508, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541955508-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu temple ", "text": "Pashupatinath is a big Hindu temple, and it is always crowded. But the tourists, who are not Hindu, cannot enter inside. There is a small hill on the opposite side of the river, and from this place you can take a nice pictures of the temple.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "33E3BE3C46C70801BA65DBC8DF9FA0F8", "name": "Kimitaka Sho", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/kimitakas", "username": "kimitakas", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0b/97/68/8c/kimitaka-s.jpg", "contribution_count": 16595, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 298564, "location_name": "Kyoto", "location_name_detailed": "Kyoto, Japan"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/4f/eb/e1/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/4f/eb/e2/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/4f/eb/e3/photo2jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-11-19", "published_at_date": "2017-11-20"}, {"review_id": 541810626, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541810626-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very special place", "text": "It was a privilege to watch a very public cremation ceremony in this sacred place. A very sympathetic way to honor the dead.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "894A550B73FC281F660E9A2100A22113", "name": "janina776", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/janina776", "username": "janina776", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f0/48/default-avatar-2020-15.jpg", "contribution_count": 27, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186369, "location_name": "Somerset", "location_name_detailed": "Somerset, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-18", "published_at_date": "2017-11-19"}, {"review_id": 541689302, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541689302-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Dedicated to Lord Shiva The Crematoria", "text": "Visited The Pashupatinath Temple. Dedicated to Lord Shiva, Pashupatinath is one of the four most important religious sites in Asia for devotees of Shiva. Built in the 5th century and later renovated by Malla kings, For tourist its pilgrimage place we did pooja lord shiva there and sat for long time.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "400585B2AA33F527AA7AB9882B7D2517", "name": "Jigneshpatel277", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Jigneshpatel277", "username": "Jigneshpatel277", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/60/default-avatar-2020-64.jpg", "contribution_count": 68, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297608, "location_name": "Ahmedabad", "location_name_detailed": "Ahmedabad, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-18", "published_at_date": "2017-11-18"}, {"review_id": 541634693, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541634693-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A tourist must do", "text": "I took my family back to see this on this holiday, it is a realty check on what life is, and what happens after. I would recommend a mask while sightseeing, the air pollution is terrible and the cremation fires add to this. Tip to pay 10 dollars and get a guide", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "64E6B1BD37AC3FCCBF96B64D87D273AE", "name": "Slentp", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Slentp", "username": "Slentp", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/14/09/2f/slentp.jpg", "contribution_count": 36, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 659071, "location_name": "Labrador", "location_name_detailed": "Labrador, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-17", "published_at_date": "2017-11-18"}, {"review_id": 541319076, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541319076-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu´s big temple", "text": "The most famous and big temple is pashupati nath which is situated on the banks of the holy River Bagmati.It is god shiva 's temple.shiva is biggeat god of hindu people.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3A7CC60A70D68873A64B31AC7B65829E", "name": "Emirua", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Emirua", "username": "Emirua", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e4/59/default-avatar-2020-49.jpg", "contribution_count": 10, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-11-16", "published_at_date": "2017-11-16"}, {"review_id": 541230015, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r541230015-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "The Temple on the banks of the Bagmati River", "text": "During my visit to the Pashupatinath Temple complex, there was much to see and experience that was one of the highlights of my journey through Nepal. I learned that this Temple is dedicated to Pashupati, another manifestation of the Hindu deity, Shiva. This manifestation of that of the \"lord of the animals.\" Representations of Shiva were found in the phallus statues that were located in the shrines along the hill at the Temple complex.\n\nAs one of the holiest Hindu sites in Nepal, only Hindus are allowed in the actual temple. However, there is much to see around the Temple complex. There is the Bagmati River, along which funeral pyres burn while family and loved ones mourn the passing of the deceased. There are monkeys galore as well as Sadus—holy men, some of whom solicit photographs, for a small fee. They can be identified by the brightly colored clothes and painted faces.\n\nI found this to be more of a somber place than some of the other temples I visited in Nepal, but a great place for reflection.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2D49736F0BFC0D859F997773ED2F3822", "name": "jonahNJ", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/jonahNJ", "username": "jonahNJ", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/02/3c/b0/e9/jonahnj.jpg", "contribution_count": 11524, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 46724, "location_name": "Pennington", "location_name_detailed": "Pennington, New Jersey"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/69/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/72/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/83/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/8d/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/96/monkeys-along-the-bagmati.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/9a/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/a5/shrine.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/b6/shrine.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/d0/shrines.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/e1/shrine.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/48/de/e5/shrines.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-11-15", "published_at_date": "20